@startuml
title Figure 4: System Administrator - Authentication & User Management

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam dpi 150
cduenceMessageAlign center

actor "System\nAdministrator" as Admin
participant "System" as System
database "Database" as DB
participant "Authentication" as Auth
participant "Email\nService" as Email

== Login ==
Admin -> System: Login Request\n(email, password)
System -> Auth: Validate Credentials
Auth -> DB: Check User\n(email, password_hash)
DB --> Auth: User Found\n(role=ADMIN)
Auth --> System: Authentication Success\n(JWT Token)
System --> Admin: Login Successful\n(Redirect to Dashboard)

== User Management ==

Admin -> System: Create User\n(Employee ID, Name, Email,\nPhone, Role, Department)
System -> System: Generate Temporary\nPassword (8 chars)
System -> System: Hash Password\n(BCrypt)
System -> DB: Insert User Record\n(isFirstLogin=true)
DB --> System: User Created\n(User ID)
System -> Email: Send Welcome Email\n(Credentials + Login URL)
Email --> Admin: Email Sent Confirmation
System --> Admin: User Created Successfully\n(Show Employee ID)

Admin -> System: View All Users
System -> DB: SELECT * FROM users
DB --> System: User List\n(All Departments)
System --> Admin: Display Users Table\n(Name, Email, Role, Department)

Admin -> System: Update User\n(Change Role/Department)
System -> DB: UPDATE users\nSET role, department
DB --> System: User Updated
System -> Email: Send Notification\n(Role/Department Changed)
System --> Admin: User Updated Successfully

Admin -> System: Deactivate User\n(User ID)
System -> DB: UPDATE users\nSET isActive=false
DB --> System: User Deactivated
System -> DB: INSERT audit_log\n(Action: USER_DEACTIVATED)
System --> Admin: User Deactivated\nSuccessfully

@enduml
